# Devnet sandbox build (`npm run build:devnet` / `deploy:devnet`) — deployed only to
# otchub.dev/devnet + otchub.dev/drip (see ../wrangler.jsonc `env.devnet`). Public values only,
# safe to commit: a public RPC endpoint and the devnet program id, both already public knowledge
# on-chain.
#
# For a faster/more reliable RPC than the public devnet endpoint, override in `.env.devnet.local`
# (gitignored, never committed) — e.g. a Helius devnet URL:
# VITE_HUB_RPC_URL=https://devnet.helius-rpc.com/?api-key=<HELIUS_API_KEY>
VITE_HUB_RPC_URL=https://api.devnet.solana.com
VITE_HUB_CLUSTER=devnet
VITE_HUB_PROGRAM_ID=7c5oPs9GvX8vrC5jVFketNx1ZLuPs7HeH8Qc4XJx7b7i
# Cloudflare Turnstile public site key for the /drip faucet's bot-abuse challenge — public by
# design, pairs with the TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY Worker secret (see workers/faucet.ts). Left unset
# here on purpose: set the real key in `.env.devnet.local` (gitignored) once a widget exists for
# otchub.dev, then `wrangler secret put TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY --env devnet`.
# VITE_TURNSTILE_SITE_KEY=
